0. THE DEFINITION

INTELLIGENCE : NOT ACTING FROM A DISTORTED PERCEPTION

THE EGO : FEAR, DESIRE

Most definitions of intelligence are positive — the ability to solve problems, achieve goals, adapt. This one is negative. It locates the failure mode instead of the capacity:

The obstacle is not lack of power. The obstacle is distortion.

Fear distorts perception by making threats visible where none exist. Desire distorts perception by making what you want seem true. Both are preference overriding observation. That is the mechanism.

Everything in this white paper is derived from this definition. The four walls the AI narrative collided with are four faces of one failure: preference overriding observation. The architecture is an attempt to build a system that does not act from distorted perception — at the level of its own operation.

What the architecture can do: refuse when observation is absent. Bound its behavior to a finite, ROM-burned action space. Make every decision auditable.

What it cannot do: make the humans perceive clearly. That is the residual, and it is named.

