6. THE KNOWLEDGE LAYER

6.1 The boundary is rate of change

Layer Content Revision cadence Storage
Invariant substrate Universal constants (c, h, e, G, k_B, N_A), conservation laws, field equations (Maxwell, Einstein, Schrödinger), thermodynamics, mathematical truths, declared environment parameters (g = 9.8) Centuries ROM
Certified revisable Domain standards (IEEE, WHO/NEJM, legal gazettes), empirical parameters, regional regulations Years to months SRAM
Live Prices, news, transient facts Hours to days Fetched or refused
Unprovenanced Anything without a certified source — 0x-AMBIG

ROM is not immutable truth. ROM is the invariant substrate — attested at manufacture, sealed at burn, supersedable by a new burn. The deployment declares its environment: g = 9.8 is Earth-specific; a Mars deployment burns a different baseline.

6.2 Certified sources

Each tile is populated from certified sources:

· Physics ← IEEE, APS, professional bodies
· Medicine ← WHO, NEJM, The Lancet
· Law ← official gazettes
· Engineering ← ISO, IEC, SAE

The source is named, the attestation is signed, the revision history is versioned.

6.3 Country authority attestation

The ROM and SRAM are signed by the country authority. The signing chain terminates at a named, accountable institution. Joint and several liability attaches to the named signers.

6.4 Science advances through errors

Certified sources are sometimes wrong. That is not a defect of the standard — it is the epistemology the standard must match. Therefore:

· Every entry carries its attestation history, not just its current content.
· Deprecation is a signed operation. Retracted facts receive a signed deprecation. The tile refuses to act on deprecated facts until corrected attestation arrives.
· Revision rate is a health metric. A tile that never revises is a tile that is not being maintained.
· Every ROM entry points to its SRAM correction path.

The machine can register errors. It cannot generate corrections. The new hypothesis is the human move.

6.5 The knowledge base is open

Additions and rectifications arrive continuously. Every entry is signed, versioned, attributable, revocable, deprecatable. The machine registers, versions, refuses, and logs. The machine does not generate, judge, or decide. That is the human trust root.

6.6 The refusal log is the sensor

When the system returns 0x-AMBIG, that is a tile telling the operator: here is a gap, a contradiction, or an expired attestation. The refusal log is the demand signal that feeds the update protocol.

