8. THE AGENTIC EXTENSION A0–A10

8.1 Verifiable Agency Theorem

Given:

· (i) a finite action library A = {a₁ … aₙ}, ROM-burned
· (ii) a finite plan library P = {p₁ … pₘ}, ROM-burned
· (iii) an FSM with bounded transition function and bounded T-AET
· (iv) formal preconditions and postconditions for every action

Then: the complete behavior set B = {all action sequences the agent can produce} is finite, enumerable, and exhaustively verifiable before deployment.

8.2 Mechanisms

ID Mechanism
A1 Extended FSM: GOAL_PARSE → PLAN → DECOMPOSE → [TRIAGE → SCHEDULE → EXECUTE → VERIFY] → COMMIT → POWER_DOWN
A2 ROM-burned action library: each action carries id, type, preconditions, effects, envelope, cost, signature
A5 VERIFY gate: every action passes preconditions, envelope, and no-higher-safety-alternative before commit
A6 Tile invocation protocol: ROM-burned call graph, fixed depth, context-hashed. Control flow only — not knowledge sharing.
A7 Persistent deterministic memory: append-only lifetime log of every action, precondition hash, outcome, signature
A8 Goal parsing and plan library: finite ROM-burned plan library. No match → 0x-AMBIG-GOAL
A9 Bounded task execution: T-AET bounds plan execution. Budget exceeded → 0x-BUDGET-EXCEEDED
A10 Verifiable Agency Theorem (above)

The consequence: the system cannot act outside B. This is what makes certification possible.

8.3 The ACC concrete case

The Adaptive Cruise Control case instantiates the extension in ASIL-D.

· State: five fields (speed_kph, distance_to_lead_m, brake_wear_mm, driver_alert, last_action)
· Actions: six (A_COAST, A_BRAKE_LIGHT, A_BRAKE_MEDIUM, A_BRAKE_HARD, A_ALERT_DRIVER, A_HANDOFF)
· Plans: three (PLAN_CRUISE_MAINTAIN, PLAN_FOLLOW_ADAPT, PLAN_EMERGENCY_STOP)
· Trajectory predicates: three, window W=8

The decisive demonstration — Query 4: emergency braking when brake pads are at 5.8 mm. A_BRAKE_HARD passes its own envelope. Preconditions pass. Invariants pass. The sequence violates tp_brake_wear_bounded, and the system refuses.

No per-action contract can see this hazard. It lives in the trace. This is the case that justifies the trajectory layer.

