14. CONCLUSION

The transformer was built to guess a sentence. The industry scaled it into a cosmology, hit four physical walls, renamed the walls, renamed the system, and handed the system a uniform.

The walls are one wall. Distortion: preference overriding observation. Fear and desire bending perception. The definition from 1987, stated in machine terms.

ST-T1024 is not a better narrative. It is a different building.

It solves energy, water, hallucination, and liability by architecture. It supplies a portable, machine-verifiable language for inter-organizational admission. It derives its refusal floor from first principles. It governs — does not solve — knowledge acquisition, with a rate-graded substrate, signed attestation, three update clocks, and a refusal log that closes the loop. It scales to arbitrary tile count because tile independence is architectural, not conventional.

It names its residuals: the human trust root, capture of the authority, cross-border mapping, adversarial drift, multi-agent convergence, silicon validation, signer throughput, and the consistency of duplicated facts.

A standard that names its residuals is one that can be trusted. A standard that hides them is one that cannot.

The work is not complete. But the architecture is coherent, the theorem is clean, the first domain is demonstrated, and the standard is proposed.

